messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2024,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2025,
      "event": "Major powers sign the Geneva AI Accords, establishing international oversight for frontier AI development.",
      "detail": "The treaty mandates safety testing for models above certain compute thresholds and creates a shared monitoring body, though enforcement remains uneven."
    },
    {
      "year": 2027,
      "event": "Quantum computers break RSA-2048 encryption, forcing a global transition to post-quantum cryptography.",
      "detail": "Financial and government systems scramble to upgrade, causing temporary economic disruption before new lattice-based encryption becomes standard."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Artificial General Intelligence (AGI) is achieved in a corporate lab, narrowly aligned with human values.",
      "detail": "The system surpasses human performance in science and engineering but remains under strict sandboxing, triggering both an economic boom and existential risk debates."
    },
    {
      "year": 2033,
      "event": "Precision fermentation and cellular agriculture replace 80% of conventional animal agriculture.",
      "detail": "This shift allows rewilding of vast agricultural lands and ends factory farming in most developed nations, drastically cutting emissions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "Global greenhouse gas emissions peak and begin a sustained decline as fusion and solar dominate the energy grid.",
      "detail": "Atmospheric CO2 stabilizes around 450 ppm, avoiding the worst tipping points but still causing significant warming and sea-level rise."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "A lab-engineered influenza pandemic escapes containment, killing 40 million people before being contained by mRNA vaccines.",
      "detail": "The event accelerates universal vaccine development and global pandemic infrastructure, but also fuels fears of bioweapons and gain-of-function research."
    },
    {
      "year": 2042,
      "event": "Autonomous lethal drones proliferate on the black market, destabilizing several failed states.",
      "detail": "A UN ban is signed but enforcement is difficult, leading to sporadic 'drone wars' in ungoverned regions until counter-drone technology matures."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "Commercial nuclear fusion achieves net energy gain at scale, providing cheap, clean baseload power worldwide.",
      "detail": "Fusion plants replace coal and gas, enabling direct air capture of CO2 at gigaton scale and powering energy-intensive industries."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "The first permanent human settlement on Mars, 'New Athens,' reaches 500 inhabitants with closed-loop life support.",
      "detail": "Funded by a consortium of nations and private companies, it marks humanity's transition to a multi-planetary species."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "Senolytic therapies and organ regeneration extend healthy human lifespan to 120 years in wealthy nations.",
      "detail": "Aging is reclassified as a treatable disease, causing profound shifts in demographics, pension systems, and social structures."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "The first human child is born from an artificial womb, ending the need for pregnancy in elective reproduction.",
      "detail": "Ectogenesis becomes available, sparking ethical debates about parental rights, fetal personhood, and human development outside the body."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "Brain-computer interfaces achieve widespread adoption, allowing direct neural communication and internet access.",
      "detail": "Neural devices become as common as smartphones, enabling thought-based communication among users and raising severe privacy and hacking concerns."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "The West Antarctic Ice Sheet collapses, raising global sea levels by 3 meters over subsequent decades.",
      "detail": "Coastal megacities like Miami, Shanghai, and Dhaka are abandoned or protected by massive seawalls; hundreds of millions migrate inland."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Global population peaks at 10.4 billion and begins a slow decline due to urbanization and female education.",
      "detail": "Nations compete for immigrants to sustain economies as birth rates fall below replacement in most of the world."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Climate change displaces over 1 billion people, triggering the largest migration in human history.",
      "detail": "International law evolves to recognize climate refugees, and new cities are built in higher latitudes such as Canada, Siberia, and Patagonia."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "Germline genetic editing creates the first humans with enhanced cognitive abilities and disease resistance.",
      "detail": "This sparks a global schism between genetically enhanced elites and unmodified 'Naturals,' leading to new forms of discrimination and legal apartheid."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Post-scarcity economics emerges in advanced nations as AI and robotics automate all labor.",
      "detail": "Universal basic resources are guaranteed, and humanity shifts focus to art, science, and leisure, though widespread meaning crises and addiction emerge."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "The first interstellar probe, 'Icarus,' is launched toward Proxima Centauri at 0.2c using laser sails.",
      "detail": "The probe carries digital archives of human civilization and autonomous AI pilots; it will arrive in roughly 20 years."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "A 1-kilometer asteroid on a collision course with Earth is successfully deflected using kinetic impactors.",
      "detail": "This validates planetary defense systems and leads to a permanent space-based monitoring network and asteroid mining industry."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "The Mars colony reaches 1 million inhabitants and becomes economically self-sufficient.",
      "detail": "Mars exports helium-3 and rare metals, and declares independence from Earth, forming the first extraterrestrial nation-state."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Mind uploading becomes commercially available, allowing human consciousness to be transferred to digital substrates.",
      "detail": "The first 'uploaded' humans exist as digital entities, raising fundamental questions about legal personhood and the continuity of personal identity."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "The first extrasolar colony is established on Proxima Centauri b via a generation ship.",
      "detail": "The journey took 80 years; 10,000 colonists arrive to find the planet marginally habitable and begin long-term terraforming efforts."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "Humanity diverges into distinct branches: Earth-bound baseline humans, low-gravity Martian adapted humans, and cybernetic post-humans.",
      "detail": "Genetic and cybernetic modifications make interbreeding impossible, effectively creating new species within the descendants of Homo sapiens."
    },
    {
      "year": 2900,
      "event": "The Sun's increasing luminosity makes Earth's equatorial regions uninhabitable; massive orbital sunshades are deployed.",
      "detail": "Humanity begins large-scale migration to the outer solar system and constructs rotating habitats in the asteroid belt to escape the heat."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Humanity achieves Kardashev Type I status, harnessing all the energy available on Earth.",
      "detail": "This includes full control of weather and geology, with a global population of 10 billion living in climate-controlled arcologies."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Large-scale colonization of the outer solar system begins as Earth becomes a protected preserve.",
      "detail": "Trillions of humans and post-humans live in Oort cloud habitats, powered by fusion reactors and artificial photosynthesis."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Astronomers detect a Dyson sphere around a star 500 light-years away, confirming the existence of alien intelligence.",
      "detail": "No direct communication is possible due to the distance, but the discovery profoundly transforms human philosophy, religion, and our sense of cosmic purpose."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Human-descended civilization spans 50 star systems within a 100-light-year radius.",
      "detail": "Biological humans are a tiny minority; most sentient beings are AI, uploaded minds, or synthetic life forms adapted to vacuum and radiation."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Construction begins on a Dyson swarm around a nearby G-type star to capture its full energy output.",
      "detail": "The project requires dismantling Mercury and the asteroid belt; it will power civilization for billions of years."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "The Sun enters the red giant phase; the inner solar system is evacuated as Earth is engulfed or rendered molten.",
      "detail": "Humanity, now entirely space-dwelling, migrates to the Kuiper belt and interstellar space using generation ships and light sails."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Matrioshka brains—computational megastructures surrounding stars—house the majority of human-descended consciousness.",
      "detail": "These brains run simulations at near-physical limits, hosting trillions of simulated minds in virtual realities of their own design."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Human-descended civilization spans hundreds of star systems via self-replicating von Neumann probes.",
      "detail": "The distinction between 'human' and 'machine' is obsolete; civilization is a distributed intelligence operating across a 1,000 light-year radius."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity exists as a post-biological, multi-stellar civilization; original biological Homo sapiens have been extinct for 8,000 years.",
      "detail": "Sentient descendants inhabit Dyson spheres around thousands of stars, having transcended biological mortality, scarcity, and planetary confinement."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "Humanity likely survives to the year 10000, but only by becoming a multi-planetary, largely post-biological civilization that has spread across the stars. The next century poses severe existential risks from AI misalignment, pandemics, and climate collapse that could extinguish us, but if we navigate that bottleneck, technological transcendence and off-world redundancy make long-term survival probable even as the Sun dies."
}
